@startuml
title Option C — detailed JWT and canonical identity resolution
autonumber

actor "Browser / curl" as Client
participant "Cloudflare Access" as Access
collections "Access JWKS" as AccessJWKS
participant "Worker" as Worker
database "Worker ES256\nprivate JWK" as WorkerKey
collections "Supabase\npublic JWK set" as SupabaseKeys
participant "Data API\n(PostgREST)" as API
participant "Resolver RPC\nSECURITY DEFINER" as RPC
database "user_identities" as Identities
database "app_users" as Users
database "items + RLS" as Items

== Access authentication ==
Client -> Access: GET /items
alt Access session absent
  Access --> Client: login / OTP
  Client -> Access: verified identity
end
Access -> Worker: request + JWT A in Cf-Access-Jwt-Assertion
note right of Worker
JWT A: Cloudflare-issued, RS256
sub=y (provider identity)
email, iss, aud, exp
end note

Worker -> AccessJWKS: fetch or cached signing keys
AccessJWKS --> Worker: public keys
Worker -> Worker: jwtVerify(A)\nrequire expected iss + aud
alt A invalid / expired / wrong audience
  Worker --> Client: 403
else A valid
  == Temporary identity-resolution JWT ==
  Worker -> WorkerKey: import private ES256 JWK
  Worker -> Worker: mint JWT B; TTL 300 seconds
  note right of Worker
JWT B header: ES256, kid=<Supabase key id>
JWT B claims:
sub=y; email=<verified Access email>
cf_access_sub=y; role=authenticated
bridge_stage=identity_resolution; iat; exp
end note
  Worker -> API: POST resolver RPC\nAuthorization: Bearer B
  API -> SupabaseKeys: choose kid; verify ES256 signature
  SupabaseKeys --> API: B trusted
  API -> RPC: execute as authenticated
  RPC -> RPC: read auth.uid()=y\nread auth.jwt()->>'email'
  alt active cloudflare_access:y mapping exists
    RPC -> Identities: select canonical user_id x
    Identities --> RPC: x
  else no mapping exists
    RPC -> Users: find x by normalized verified email
    alt old GoTrue user was backfilled
      Users --> RPC: existing x
    else brand-new Access user
      RPC -> Users: insert app_users(email); generate x
      Users --> RPC: new x
    end
    RPC -> Identities: insert cloudflare_access:y -> x
  end
  RPC --> API: x
  API --> Worker: x
  == Final CRUD JWT ==
  Worker -> Worker: mint JWT C; TTL 300 seconds
  note right of Worker
JWT C header: ES256, same kid
JWT C claims:
sub=x (canonical ownership identity)
email=<verified Access email>; cf_access_sub=y
role=authenticated; iat; exp
No bridge_stage claim
end note
  Worker -> API: items CRUD\nAuthorization: Bearer C
  API -> SupabaseKeys: choose kid; verify ES256 signature
  SupabaseKeys --> API: C trusted
  API -> Items: execute as authenticated
  Items -> Items: auth.uid()=x; items.user_id=x
  Items --> API: permitted rows / mutation result
  API --> Worker: result
  Worker --> Client: API response only
end

note over Client,Items
JWT B and JWT C exist inside Worker memory and go only to Supabase.
They are never returned in an HTTP response.
end note
@enduml
